('115.14.b.3.E',3,'A good friend will...','["ignore you when you are sad", "spread your secrets", "listen and keep your trust", "tease you"]'::jsonb,2,'Good friends are trustworthy.','original'),
('115.14.b.3.F',3,'A respectful way to talk to a teacher is to...','["talk over them", "shout answers", "roll your eyes", "raise your hand and wait"]'::jsonb,3,'Respect shows in how you speak.','original'),
('115.14.b.3.F',3,'When a family member is speaking, it is respectful to...','["listen without interrupting", "laugh at them", "yell", "walk away"]'::jsonb,0,'Listening shows respect.','original'),
('115.14.b.3.G',3,'A friend crosses their arms and looks away. Their nonverbal cue may mean they feel...','["hungry", "upset", "silly", "excited"]'::jsonb,1,'Body language gives clues.','original'),
('115.14.b.3.G',3,'A classmate''s voice shakes and they say "I''m fine." Their verbal and nonverbal cues may not match, so you could...','["ignore them", "laugh at them", "ask kindly if they are okay", "tell everyone"]'::jsonb,2,'Check in with care.','original'),
('115.14.b.3.H',3,'To repair a broken friendship, you can...','["break their things", "ignore the person forever", "spread rumors", "apologize and listen"]'::jsonb,3,'Apologies repair relationships.','original'),
('115.14.b.3.H',3,'To prevent a friendship from breaking, you should...','["talk about problems early", "ignore your friend", "keep secrets that hurt", "argue loudly"]'::jsonb,0,'Early talking prevents big fights.','original'),
